WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.033
We're here with
Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.267
So I feel like for two years

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.801
we talked about
who's going to win the House.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.667
And then for weeks we covered
who's going to be the Speaker.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:12.400
And then since Kevin McCarthy
got the gavel, I -- nothing.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.901
I feel like we
barely hear anything.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.834
For someone
who's up close to it,

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:20.133
what do you feel the GOP
is trying to do with this power?

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.734
-Yeah, well, first of all,
you're absolutely right.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:28.767
I believe this is the least
productive first three months

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:31.501
under almost any Speaker

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:32.934
potentially in the history
of the United States,

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:35.200
if not in modern
political history.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.400
And I think it's because,
you know,

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.067
they talked a lot
about winning,

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:44.033
but they didn't really plan
for what they wanted to do.

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:45.467
So they're kind of
sitting around

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.601
and they're looking
at state legislatures

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:50.067
and they're like,
"Maybe we can ban books."

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:55.067
And we say, "No,
you should not do that."

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:58.968
And I think
they're, you know --

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:02.100
I'm so grateful that we have
a Democratic Senate

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.434
and that folks turned out

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:06.200
and elected so many incredible
members of the Senate

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.400
to be a kind
of a stop on that.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.000
But I just think
they don't really know.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.033
And I also think Kevin McCarthy
promised so many people

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:17.834
so many different things
that he cannot possibly govern

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:20.501
with all these pre-commitments
that he's made.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:24.400
-A way to, I guess,
seem like you're doing something

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.300
while also not governing
is to complain about wokeism

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.501
and how it affects
everything from bank

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:33.000
collapses to the way
our military is being run.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.367
Is that -- Are you in actual
meetings and committee hearings

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.634
where that is the sort of
topic du jour?

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.334
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:45.934
House Republicans held an
entire -- an entire hearing

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:49.300
on "wokeism"
in the federal government

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.968
and federal employment policies.
And so I'm looking at it.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:55.067
I'm like, "What is so woke
that has them so outraged?"

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:56.567
And I look through this list
and I'm like,

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:59.901
oh, paying members
of the Forest Service

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:02.667
more than a Walmart greeter,

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:05.267
using remote work
for people with disabilities

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.067
and people who live
in rural areas,

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.067
you know, healthcare,

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:13.300
and like --
it's just a catch-all term

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.934
that they use for anything
that they don't like.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.334
-And I guess
one of the problems

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:19.033
is when they actually get to
legislating on things like that,

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.434
even their constituents

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.601
wouldn't want to lose things
like healthcare,

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.534
especially when
they realize wokeism

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:25.634
has nothing to do with it.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:26.868
-Yeah, I think
that's why they have to

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.334
call it wokeism

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.834
because if they actually told
their constituents,

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:34.767
"Hey, we don't want the Forest
Service folks to get paid well,"

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.968
people would be like,
"Why do you want to do that?"

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:41.300
And so I think they have to
brand it as all this stuff.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.400
And I mean,
they'll say it often.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.267
I was on the floor of a debate
around some of their work

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:50.868
in trying to ban books and they
call it "parental rights"

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:54.901
but they try to package this
and use misdirection

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.234
to say "we want parents
to be more involved

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.601
and have more of a say
in their school."

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:02.334
Well, if you want that,
maybe let's create a society

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:04.067
where parents aren't working
two jobs

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.567
so that they can be
more involved

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:06.834
with their kids in school.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:08.501
[ Applause ]

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:13.033
Instead of trying
to tell people

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:17.300
that trans kids should not have
a safe place to get an education

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.968
or tell their parents
what to do.

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:22.801
I mean, it's, you know,
I think it speaks to the fact

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:25.701
that despite no matter
what happens with Donald Trump,

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:29.634
Trumpism is still alive.
And we've seen it recently.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.300
There was just a vote

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.968
in the Tennessee
state legislature to expel

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:39.367
three Democratic representatives
in their legislature

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:43.133
because they had the audacity
to stand up and protest

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:44.467
for gun-safety legislation

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:47.133
because the state of Tennessee
was not acting enough.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:50.868
And so instead
of having vigorous debate,

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:53.868
the folks who accuse people
of silencing

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:56.234
are the ones who are silencing
and expelling.

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:59.300
The folks who are accusing
people of intimidation,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.968
like Marjorie
Taylor Greene today.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.634
You know, we have --
New York City Public Advocate

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.868
Jumaane Williams is blowing
a whistle while she was talking.

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:08.000
I mean, we all have our First
Amendment right, right?

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.901
She goes around
calling this intimidation.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:14.467
And it's so often
this politics of projection

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.934
in order to get you
to become defensive

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:20.100
about what this person --
defensive towards yourself

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.801
about what the other person
is actually doing,

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.033
and we just need to move
out of that space

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.968
because I think
what most people just want

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:30.067
is for us to actually
accomplish something

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.634
as a government
that helps working people.

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:33.968
-You have also,

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.901
or I should say
the GOP has also promised

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:39.334
to get to the bottom
of the Biden crime family

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:42.267
and their term, not mine.
-Yeah.

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:44.667
-It does not seem
as though, you know, again,

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:47.901
as you said, three months,
no breaking news.

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:51.000
-Yeah. I mean, I think --
they've tried, you know.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.934
They had that big
Twitter, Hunter Biden hearing

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.734
and they're like,
"We got him."

00:04:56.734 --> 00:05:00.200
And then the thing
about hearings is that

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.200
they're not Republican
press conferences.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.267
You have 50 Democrats that are
also or however many Democrats

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.133
in the committee
that are also seated on that.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.200
And they can real-time
fact-check you,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.567
unlike Fox News,
as a "safe space" for them.

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:14.267
You know, you can get
fact-checked in real time.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.167
You will be debated
in real time.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:21.133
And they have operated
in this insular environment

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.400
that affirms them,
no matter how true or false,

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.167
anything they say
is that now

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:27.901
that they're actually
in a House majority

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:29.534
and they have to
actually call hearings

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:31.534
and they actually
have to legislate

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:34.234
and they actually have
to be called on things

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:35.801
when they're not true,

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.267
they're like, "Wait, this
doesn't feel like

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:38.834
Tucker Carlson to me."

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:44.901
It's like, no, baby, this is the
U.S. House of Representatives.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:46.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-There you go.

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.400
Well, if there's any lesson

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.367
they take away from that,
I hope that's it.

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:52.868
Hey, what a pleasure
to have you back here.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:54.934
It's always -- to have
a New Yorker here, especially

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:58.567
one -- the beautiful --
from the beautiful LaGuardia.

00:05:58.567 --> 00:06:00.534
I mean, the most beautiful
airport in the whole world.

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.200
-Look at the fountain
when you go.
-Look at the fountain.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.100
-Book your next flight.
-It's gorgeous.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.334
-It's worth flying from Europe

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:08.667
just to land at JFK, drive
to LaGuardia.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.767
Look at it. Drive back to JFK,
go back to Europe.

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:13.667
-What I will say, though,
is Moynihan Train Hall --

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.434
Let's put another one
for public transit over there.

00:06:15.434 --> 00:06:17.100
The new train hall, Amtrak.
I love it too.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.534
-The Moynihan Train Hall is
great.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:20.734
This is very exciting.

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.200
You know, things have
really turned around

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.701
since you got here.
You guys, give it up for

00:06:23.701 --> 00:06:25.667
Congresswoman Alexandria
Ocasio-Cortez.

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:27.300
-We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

